INT. BARBERSHOP - GHOST TOWN OF DRY CREEK - NOON

Dust on every surface. One chair, one mirror. A hand-painted sign in the window reads "SHAVE AND A HAIRCUT, TWO BITS."

NATHANIEL CROWFOOT, 50s, barber, apron over his vest, strops a razor on a leather belt. A STRANGER, 40s, black hat tipped low, sits in the chair under a white sheet. A young boy, TOMMY LIGHTFOOT, 12, sweeps the floor with a broom taller than he is.

NATHANIEL
Close shave?

STRANGER
Close.

NATHANIEL
You passing through?

STRANGER
Looking for a man.

Nathaniel lathers his brush. The boy stops sweeping.

NATHANIEL
Name?

STRANGER
Jedediah Kane.

The brush stops mid-air. Tommy looks at Nathaniel. Nathaniel looks at the mirror, at the stranger's eyes.

NATHANIEL
Never heard of him.

JEDEDIAH
That's funny. Folks say he gets his hair cut here.

NATHANIEL
Folks say a lot of things.

The bell on the door jingles. SHERIFF AMOS WHITCOMBE, 60s, steps in, hand on his holster.

SHERIFF
Nathaniel. Boy. Everyone breathing?

NATHANIEL
Barely.

SHERIFF
(to Jedediah)
That's an interesting hat.

JEDEDIAH
It keeps the sun off.

SHERIFF
There's no sun in here.

JEDEDIAH
It keeps my thoughts in.

The sheriff draws. Jedediah flings the sheet and rises from the chair, razor in his hand. Nathaniel catches his wrist. They tangle. The gun fires into the ceiling. Plaster rains.

Tommy dives behind the broom. Nathaniel wrenches the razor free and presses it to Jedediah's throat. The sheriff levels his pistol at both.

SHERIFF (CONT'D)
Nathaniel, let him go.

NATHANIEL
Which one?

SHERIFF
Either.

Beat. Nathaniel lowers the razor. Wipes it on his apron.

NATHANIEL
Shave's on the house.
